window.docContents[250].resolve({"/part-4-frameworks/ch14-enlargements/#ch14-enlargements":{"contents":"Countable ultrapowers over \\mathbb{N} create unlimited numbers and infinitesimals for countable families of constraints—but what if X is an uncountable topological space, a vast group, or an infinite-dimensional normed space?\n\nA binary relation R is concurrent (or finitely satisfiable) if for every finite collection x_1, \\dots, x_k \\in \\mathrm{dom}(R), there exists some y simultaneously satisfying R(x_1, y) \\land \\cdots \\land R(x_k, y). A nonstandard framework is an Enlargement if for every concurrent relation R, there exists a single nonstandard witness b satisfying {}^*R({}^*x, b) for all standard x \\in \\mathrm{dom}(R) at once!\n\nLook at what one enlargement witness b gives immediately:\n\n* Take R(x, F) :\\iff x \\in F \\land F \\text{ is finite} on an infinite set A: enlargement produces a hyperfinite set F^+ \\subseteq {}^*A containing {}^*x for every standard element x \\in A!* Take R(U, y) :\\iff y \\in U on the open neighbourhoods U of a point p in any topological space: enlargement produces a point inside the monad \\mu(p) = \\bigcap_{U \\in \\mathcal{N}(p)} {}^*U!\n\nIn Ch14_Enlargements.lean (2,187 lines), we prove Goldblatt's Theorem 14.3.1 by constructing a fine ultrafilter on the directed set I = \\mathrm{Finset}(\\mathcal{C}) of finite constraint sets (extending all upper cones \\{i \\in I : i_0 \\subseteq i\\} via Zorn's Lemma), proving unconditionally that every mathematical universe admits an enlargement (exists_enlargement)!\n\nsection\nopen Goldblatt.Ch14\n\n-- Fine ultrafilters and Goldblatt's Theorem 14.3.1 (Existence of Enlargements):\n#check @isConcurrent_iff_hasFIP_slices\n#check @theorem_14_3_1_single_concurrent\n#check @theorem_14_3_1_hyperfinite_approx\n#check @universalUltrapowerEnlargement_isEnlargement\n#check @exists_enlargement\nend\n\n\n","context":"Lectures on the Hyperreals — Interactive Lean 4 & Spatial Edition\u0009Part IV — Nonstandard Frameworks, Enlargements & Saturation","header":"4.2. Chapter 14: Concurrent Relations & Enlargements","id":"/part-4-frameworks/ch14-enlargements/#ch14-enlargements"}});